      "text": "Dear colleagues, my name is Xian Hong, the program specialist at the Secretary of Information for All Program of UNESCO, very warm greetings to you from Paris. I'm very honored to share some of our work related to the artificial intelligence. Before going to the subject, I'd like to introduce briefly the program I work on is called the Information for All Program, created in 2001, mandated to support member states and stakeholders on information policies for building inclusive knowledge societies. We actually work on six priorities, information for development, information literacy, information preservation, information ethics, information accessibility, and multilingualism in server space. I draw your attention to UNESCO's recommendation on the ethics of artificial intelligence as the first truly global framework for the ethical use of artificial intelligence.",
